\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  blight unsettles Hong Kong. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sarah Davison \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1997\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, July 21 (Reuter) - Persistent contagion throughout Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets unsettled the Hong Kong dollar on Monday but most analysts still knocked down any suggestion of speculative weakness. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the Hong Kong dollar is likely to fall prey to speculators," said Dong Tao, economist at Schroder Securities in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Short-term interest rates soared and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards widened in Hong Kong after speculators attacked the Indonesian rupiah, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had seemed immune to speculation swirling through the region this month. \par \par \uc2  As heavy speculative selling pushed the rupiah to a new record low of 2,655 to the U.S. dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar spot rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar within a safe distance of the key psychological level of HK$7.7500. At 0500 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was back on firmer ground, trading at HK$7.7470/80 and well-linked to its 14-year-old fixed rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said any break of the HK$7.7500 level could signal a sharp slide, which was why the HKMA was determined to defend it. \par \par \uc2  But traders were tense. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is nervous," one dealer said. "Yes, definitely, everyone is nervous." \par \par \uc2  Speculators have already forced a depreciation of the Thai baht and Philippine peso, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are jittery in Malaysia and even Singapore, long considered a safe haven. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit was still weak on Monday after hitting a 38-month low in London on Friday, while the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet again to support its battered peso on Monday, which was trading at 28.35 to the U.S. dollar compared with pre-July 11 depreciation levels of 26. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht, now trading at about 30.35 to the U.S. dollar compared to pre-July 2 depreciation level of 25, was sluggish with most of the domestic market on holiday. \par \par \uc2  In Hong Kong, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards widened to 210 in the three-month and 400 in the six-month from more usual levels in the single digits, and money market rates soared. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate climbed to 6.37 percent, while the one-week Exchange Fund bill yield reached 6.53 percent compared with 5.31 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  Spreads to corresponding U.S. government paper widened sharply. \par \par \uc2  Despite the tension, analysts remained confident that the Hong Kong dollar would remain an island of stability in a sea of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil. \par \par \uc2  "Hong Kong's fundamentals are much stronger than many of the Southeast Asian economies. Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are huge even without added support from China," Tao said. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong holds at least US$63 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves while China, which has promised to defend the Hong Kong dollar if it comes under attack, has a cache of US$121 billion. \par \par \uc2  HKMA chief executive Joseph Yam has issued repeated warnings to speculators never to attack the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The territory's vast reserves and strong economic fundamentals set Hong Kong apart from some of the most troubled Asian nations now battling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, as does Yam's market credibility and that of the institution he controls. \par \par \uc2  But confidence is key in this situation and, following weakness in the Singapore dollar, there are signs of eroding confidence in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "I think (Yam's) message has been heard but because of the hectic happenings in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets investors might be just too nervous to take notice of what Mr. Yam has to say," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7l02656\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
