\par\par \b \uc2  HK/Stock Index/Amplifier -3: Baht Crisis Favors HK$ \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 1997\par 11:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  While the territory took time off commemorate the change in sovereignty, Thai authorities allowed their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the baht, to float on Wednesday, abandoning a 13-year basket arrangement in the face of increasing pressure from international markets. \par \par \uc2  The impact of the Thai move on the Hong Kong dollar was slight and on balance positive, as some investors switched to the Hong Kong dollar, which officials assure will continue being pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.80 for some time to come. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a British investment bank said that some in the market are switching to the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of its safe haven reputation in the region, but overall the effect has been minimal. \par \par \uc2  In late trading Thursday, the U.S. dollar was slightly lower against the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . quoted at HK$7.7440, compared with Friday afternoon's HK$7.7480. \par \par \uc2  The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -peg assurance came Thursday from Hong Kong's top financial official, who said that Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hasn't yet resorted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rate. \par \par \uc2  Financial Secretary Donald Tsang Yam-kuen said, 'I do not see the threat at all, and there is no question whatsoever that I am going to even consider changing the link.' \par \par \uc2  Tsang added at a briefing for reporters that 'we are watching the developments with great interest. As far as the Hong Kong dollar is concerned, it is rock solid. The Hong Kong government has not been in the market. The Hong Kong dollar is still trading on the strong side of the link.' \par \par \uc2  Tsang wouldn't discuss if the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was asked by the Bank of Thailand to exercise an existing repurchase agreement that could help it raise cash. \par \par \uc2  And the financial secretary said Hong Kong is in a stronger financial position than Thailand because of its healthy reserves, fiscal surplus and strong banking system. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0947GMT \par \par \uc2  1135 55126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7304vsw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
