\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger Midday As US$ Profit-Taking Continues \b0\par\par\uc2 226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1997\par 06:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger Wednesday on U.S. dollar profit-taking that began during the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has traded tightly between HK$7.7350 and HK$7.7365 so far Wednesday. It is trading at HK$7.7456 at 0405 GMT (12:05 a.m. EDT), down from HK$7.7477 around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  As Hong Kong dollar interest rates fell last week and earlier this week, the U.S. dollar began to climb, rising from HK$7.7410 last week to a high of HK$7.7483 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At that level, however, it ran out of steam because \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rates stopped their slide. In addition, participants feared \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar reached HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking began, dropping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below HK$7.7460 late Tuesday, mostly outside of the Hong Kong trading center. The profit-taking is continuing on a smaller scale so far Wednesday, said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a domestic bank. \par \par \uc2  She said the U.S. dollar probably won't fall below HK$7.7450 Wednesday and that buying interest may resume, taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as HK$7.7470. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0401GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6p04lnh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
