\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Hong Kong falls prey to Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  panic. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sarah Davison \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 13:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, May 16 (Reuter) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  panic filtered through the Hong Kong money market on Friday, sending interest rates skywards while \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards soared. \par \par \uc2  But the Hong Kong dollar remained rock solid in steady two-way trade, ignoring the ruckus just 46 days before this British colony reverts to Chinese control. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar closed at HK$7.7385 on Friday, flat against Thursday's close and well within its unofficial trading band of one percent either side of an enforced peg of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there's a problem in Hong Kong but there's a lot of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil in Asia and there aren't many countries that aren't affected by it," said Daniel Hemmant, Asian exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund manager at Guinness Flight Asia Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Speculative concern about the Thai baht and Malaysian ringgit sparked sudden rate action in Hong Kong when Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied publicly that it had ordered banks to cease ringgit swap, or forward, transactions with foreign banks. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards suddenly blew out to 65 in the three-month and 100 in the six-month from more usual levels of 15 and 40 respectively, widening further in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  Rates also skyrocketed, responding to a sudden 100-basis point rise in the overnight rate to 6.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  The one-week Exchange Fund bill yield closed at 6.16 percent while the two-year spread to the U.S. treasury -- considered a benchmark in Hong Kong's young and thinly-traded market -- gaped to 107 points from a more usual 30. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it appeared to have little effect at calming the market. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very nervous," one dealer said at the close. "People are concerned there will be more attacks on the Malaysian ringgit and that they will succeed. If that happens, it won't be good for Hong Kong." \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the market action in Hong Kong was a predictable knee-jerk reaction to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil in Thailand and Malaysia, where poor economic fundamentals attracted the attention of hedge funds from overseas. \par \par \uc2  "Basically this is a knee-jerk move rather than a fundamentally-based move and it'll snap back fairly quickly," said Callum Henderson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at MMS International. \par \par \uc2  Dealers seemed confident about the Hong Kong dollar, long considered a possible target for speculators on uncertainty associated with the switch to Chinese sovereignty on July 1. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of US$63.4 billion at the end of March and Hong Kong's sturdy fiscal and economic position were powerful disincentives to speculators tempted by the infectious spread of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness throughout the region, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Who dares to touch us? Not even (George) Soros dares to touch us. Everything is well prepared," one dealer said, referring to the hedge fund speculator who forced sterling out of the European exchange rate mechanism in 1992. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's situation is very different from Thailand, which is weighed under with bad debt, or Malaysia, which suffers from a wide current account deficit, he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5g05hns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
