\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Touch Weaker In Late Thursday Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch weaker from midday levels Thursday as participants continue to shore up on the strengthening U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0917 GMT (5:17 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7494, up slightly from HK$7.7492 around midday. It has traded between HK$7.7488 and HK$7.7498 so far. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in the market said they expect the 'TT,' the local term for the U.S. dollar, to test HK$7.7500 in coming days but technical resistance was keeping it just under that level. \par \par \uc2  'In the past, HK$7.7500 has been a strong resistance level. People anticipate strong resistance there,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a large European bank. \par \par \uc2  He said some participants were worried that the territory's quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the U.S. dollar below HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  '(Participants) will be quite happy to break through that level, but they are concerned the HKMA will step in,' he said. \par \par \uc2  A trader at another European bank said demand for the U.S. dollar is coming from commercial banking activity. 'I do think that commercial demand is behind (the U.S. dollar's) rise,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong Dollar Interbank Offered Rates (Hibor) were unchanged from midday levels, as were yields on Exchange Fund notes. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0931GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 4178 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4a02jnk\pa