\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger;Banks Take Profits On U.S. Dlr Positions \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 05:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Banks are taking profits on U.S. dollar positions Thursday, moving the Hong Kong dollar marginally higher from late in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading around HK$7.7492 early Thursday and has returned to that level at 0305 GMT (11:05 p.m. EDT Wednesday). At that level, it is essentially flat from around midday in the territory Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In-between the early trading and 0305 GMT, however, both large and small banks were seen selling U.S. dollars in small amounts. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank said she believes banks were taking profits after the U.S. dollar hit highs of HK$7.7497 in late Wednesday trading. \par \par \uc2  She said banks likely realized the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been facing stiff resistance as it approaches HK$7.7500 and weren't willing to see if they could push it through that level without risking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Still, as the dollar's movement so far Thursday indicate, there is still moderate interest in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it dips below HK$7.7490. The dollar briefly touched a low of HK$7.7489 just before 0245 GMT (10:45 p.m. EDT, Wednesday). \par \par \uc2  The dealer said she expects to see more movement into the Hong Kong dollar later Thursday and that the U.S. dollar could test a low of HK$7.7475. She noted that the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate (Hibor) is expected to climb later in the day as investors taking on short Hong Kong dollar positions move to cover them. \par \par \uc2  Other Hibor are generally stable, she said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0323GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 4178 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4a02iqa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
