\par\par \b \uc2  China, HK central banks to continue to cooperate. \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, March 7 (Reuter) - China will continue to cooperate with Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to assure financial stability, Chen Yuan, deputy governor of the Peoples' Bank of China, said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to cooperate with the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we are mutually dependent on each other. That cooperation will last for many, many years," Chen told Reuters Financial Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) carries out most of the functions of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- focusing on protecting the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar and banking supervision. The Peoples' Bank of China is China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We hope that our joint efforts to keep the market stable and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable will turn out to be very successful," Chen said. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong reverts to China on July 1 after more than 150 year of British colonial rule. \par \par \uc2  Under the "one country, two systems" scenario to be enshrined in the Sino-British treaty governing the handover, China and Hong Kong will maintain separate monetary systems. \par \par \uc2  China and Hong Kong have signed a bilateral repurchase agreement pact to provide liquidity in times of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability. \par \par \uc2  But Chen said cooperation between the two monetary authorities was otherwise informal. \par \par \uc2  "We don't have any specific instrument to use between us other than the repo agreement, but we already keep very close contact," he said, adding "that is the most efficient way to cooperate on market disturbances." \par \par \uc2  For example, "recently the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the exchange rate, and in the morning I got a phone call from (HKMA chief executive) Joseph Yam to apprise me of the situation," said Chen. \par \par \uc2  Chen said China had no plans in place to "bail out" Hong Kong markets in the event of a crisis, but stressed that he did not anticipate such a need. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England stepped in to help stabilise the Hong Kong dollar in 1983 when jitters about the impending handover sent what was then a free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling, Hong Kong government officials have said. \par \par \uc2  Shortly afterwards, Hong Kong pegged its dollar to the U.S. unit, a peg that has held firm since. The following year, British and Chinese negotiators signed a treaty governing the handover which served to allay some uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3708y1y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
