\par\par \b \uc2  HK Central Banker Yam Says HKMA Needs Political Autonomy \b0\par\par\uc2  By James T. Areddy \par \uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 08:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Any changes that affect the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  once China takes control of the territory must leave the quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  free from political \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  central banker Joseph Yam Chi-kwong. \par \par \uc2  His mandate is to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief executive during an interview with AP-Dow Jones this week. And Yam said he thinks that the authority's role in regulating banks and developing market infrastructure helps in realizing that goal. \par \par \uc2  The central banker - always strident in his support for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the U.S. dollar - acknowledged that he failed last month to persuade one of its biggest critics, Nobel Laureate Milton Friedman, that the link will be kept indefinitely after the political changeover on July 1. Yam also said the authority's ability to manipulate interbank liquidity means the Hong Kong system isn't a perfect example of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, although that characteristic works in the territory's best interest. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Yam indicated he is willing to see his reporting responsibility shift to the top official in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region government, and for the territory's HK$111.21 billion land fund to managed separately from the US$65.9 billion in foreign reserves invested by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The 48-year-old, who owns race horses named 'Insider' and 'Inner Circle,' and is clearly comfortable being one of Asia's key economic policy makers, also said he is a family man who is most satisfied tackling 'technical problems.' \par \par \uc2  Yam said he is aware of a danger of 'staying too long,' but wants to remain Hong Kong's central banker long after the transition in order to 'launch' the arrangements he has negotiated in recent years with the Chinese authorities. He said he could envisage taking an advisory role on the mainland sometime in the future. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-03-97 \par \par \uc2  0745GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 4201 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3501jiy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
