\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. dlr weaker, Hong Kong money fully recovered. \b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Feb 20 (Reuter) - The U.S. dollar slipped in a busy Hong Kong trading session on Thursday, but dealers said the weakness had nothing to do with the overnight death of paramount leader Deng Xiaoping. \par \par \uc2  "People are buying the yen on the Nikkei, which was much stronger," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Tokyo stock market's Nikkei 225 index closed 452.59 points higher at 19,051.71 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar stood at 123.60 late in Hong Kong, sharply weaker than early morning highs around 124.60 yen, with repeated tests of the 123.45 level expected. \par \par \uc2  Stop loss orders were reported at 123.30. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also softer against the German mark at 1.686 marks late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But Hong Kong money firmed sharply, discounting concern about Deng's death. \par \par \uc2  "Basically, the players have now discounted the news," said one analyst. "When the news finally came out, the Hong Kong dollar rose rather than fell." \par \par \uc2  The unit was trading at HK$7.7400 late on Thursday after attempting a break of the HK$7.7500 level earlier in the week when fears of Deng's demise filtered through the market. \par \par \uc2  Reports surfaced on Thursday of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  via central banks in England and China to keep the unit below the HK$7.7500 level. \par \par \uc2  "We heard U.K. banks and Chinese banks were the main sellers this morning. A lot of traders suspect they were selling on behalf of the HKMA or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China," she said. \par \par \uc2  The territory's de facto bank was also witnessed buying 10-year Exchange Fund Notes this morning to keep the market steady when the news of Deng's death broke. \par \par \uc2  "All the dealers suspect the HKMA was doing this because they were all sidelined," she said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards, or swaps, narrowed back to more usual ranges of eight basis points in the three-month and 30 basis points in the six-month after widening earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate was at 4.88 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, the spread between the three-month deposit rate was wider at 41 basis points compared to 34 points earlier in the day, with the bid at 5.50 percent against the U.S. three-month at 5.09 percent. \par \par \uc2  Government paper was stronger. \par \par \uc2  The two-year Exchange Fund Note (EFN) was yielding 5.60 percent for a spread of seven basis points against the comparable U.S. treasury at 5.67 percent. The spread was 11 points earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The 10-year EFN was at 6.80 percent for a spread of 49 basis points against the 10-year U.S. treasury at 6.88 percent. The spread was 57 basis points earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The one-week yield was 4.96 percent compared to five percent this morning. \par \par \uc2  -- Sarah Davison (852) 2843 6470 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2k005by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
