\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Concerns \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1997\par 04:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has returned to slightly stronger levels Wednesday on concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the U.S. dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between HK$7.7410 and HK$7.7419 so far Wednesday. It is quoted at HK$7.7413 at 0350 GMT, down from HK$7.7418 around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank said participants on Wednesday were 'a bit worried' that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would move in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or money markets to slow the U.S. dollar's recent rise. The dollar hit HK$7.7422 Tuesday, its highest level of the year against the Hong Kong dollar, on arbitrage activity. Participants were moving into U.S. dollar positions because U.S. dollar rates are at a premium to comparable Hong Kong dollar rates. \par \par \uc2  The arbitrage has slowed to a trickle Wednesday, and some local banks and large overseas banks have actually been buying small amounts of Hong Kong dollars, moving the home market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger. But the dealer said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns may have just been an excuse for some banks to take profits on their customer positions after the dollar rose steadily over the past week. \par \par \uc2  He and other participants said in recent days that the dollar appeared to be hitting resistance at the HK$7.7420 level and that its upward climb would be limited. \par \par \uc2  He said for the remainder of Wednesday he expects the U.S. dollar to trade tightly between HK$7.7410 and HK$7.7420. He also emphasized that the market was only concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that he hasn't seen any sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active in markets Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0346GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 4178 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1t00hpo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
