\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger On Resilient Stock Mkt, Capital Inflow \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 1996\par 05:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is slightly stronger around midday Monday as a resilient stock market and large inflows of foreign capital continue to boost demand for the local dollar, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  'We still see funds coming in and raising the weighting in the region. It's a rosy outlook for the stock market,' says a treasury chief at a Hong Kong bank. \par \par \uc2  Around 0330 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at $7.7321 (Hong Kong), down from HK$7.7325 around the same time Friday. It has traded in a range from HK$7.7323 to HK$7.7321 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is unlikely to sink below HK$7.7310 though, says the treasury chief as 'there is a very strong support there.' He reckons that the territory's de facto bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it falls beyond that level. \par \par \uc2  'It's possible the HKMA would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  using open-market buying of U.S. dollars or raising short-term rates,' he says. \par \par \uc2  But the deputy manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at another local bank says selling pressure on the Hong Kong dollar may arise when participants take mild profits from the equities market. \par \par \uc2  'The stock market is higher than last week so when people withdraw from the stock market on profit-taking, we will face some pressure,' he says. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-10-96 \par \par \uc2  0335GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 4178 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013dsae087v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{