\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weakening/Losses Seen -2: Pctg Move Very Small \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1996\par 12:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's move onto higher ground has been mostly composed and steady in 1996, but this week has gotten more intensive. \par \par \uc2  'It's not aggressive you know. It's not as if there is one aggressor,' said the number two official in the treasury department of a large European bank in Hong Kong. 'I don't think it's a major concern.' \par \par \uc2  But even this dealer said the market isn't used to such quick movement in the Hong Kong dollar, and therefore the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's grab at higher ground has gotten noticed. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar started the year around HK$7.7324, rose to HK$7.7330 by March 30, to HK$7.7341 by the end of April, closed the month of May at HK$7.7375 and crossed the HK$7.7400-mark on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In percentage terms, the U.S. dollar has gained a paltry 0.2% this year - but about half of that in five days. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.8000, a link established by cash U.S. dollar deposits with the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The peg is held in place by the money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the authority, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Joseph Yam Chi-kwong, chief executive of the authority, has often said the absolute exchange rate of the Hong Kong dollar doesn't concern him much, only the speed at which it makes its moves. \par \par \uc2  The market considers that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will permit fluctuation of no more than 1.0% from the HK$7.8000 peg. That means a tolerance level of about HK$7.7250 on the strong side, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been since late 1990. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-06-96 \par \par \uc2  1034GMT \par \par \uc2  1138 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds6e04x3l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
