\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weakens -2: Inching Higher In London Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1996\par 14:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is inching slightly higher from its local close at HK$7.7350 in London's smaller Hong Kong dollar-U.S. dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Based on quoted 'ask' prices of HK$7.7353 to HK$7.7355, the dealer says the Hong Kong dollar could weaken further during London and New York trading, the European bank's dealer says, though he doesn't expect significant movement. \par \par \uc2  The dealer says mainland banks have been joined by a small number of local investors, who would rather be holding U.S. dollar positions of maturities between one week and five months because of firm rates. \par \par \uc2  The one-week HIBOR was quoted at 5.375% late last Thursday and softened to 5.25% late last Friday in Hong Kong. It dropped further to 5.125% on Monday - a discount to the comparable U.S. dollar rate - and has held at the soft level through 1035 GMT Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month HIBOR rate has moved to 5.3125% on Wednesday from 5.46094% last Thursday and 5.41406% last Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's rise should be capped under HK$7.7360, the dealer says, with participants fearing stabilization attempts or outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the U.S. dollar continues its upward trend. \par \par \uc2  Not since Jan. 25 has the U.S. dollar breached the HK$7.7350 level. It briefly touched HK$7.7352 then on unsubstantiated reports that a Chinese official said the mainland had plans to bomb Taiwan should it not abandon its drive for international recognition. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-04-96 \par \par \uc2  1219GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4h0398s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
