\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Tad Firmer, Helped By Reduced China-Taiwan Rift \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 06:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch firmer Monday, on signs that Sino-Taiwanese tension may be easing. \par \par \uc2  At about 0510 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at $7.7315 (Hong Kong), down from HK$7.7316 around the same time Friday. \par \par \uc2  Bond yields and interbank rates have also eased Monday, because of the reduced tension. \par \par \uc2  'The force pulling rates down may be the Taiwanese stuff. That is settled now, and mainland China seems willing to hold talks,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a large local bank. 'But not much is special in the Hong Kong dollar today.' \par \par \uc2  Following Lee Teng Hui's presidential election victory in Taiwan Saturday, China has signaled it is willing to hold talks with Taiwanese authorities. Shen Guofang, China's foreign ministry spokesperson, said in a television interview Sunday that if Taiwan's leaders accept reunification, 'relations could be eased, and we could move on to discuss other things.' \par \par \uc2  Traders note that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at the high end of its range versus the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  'If (the U.S. dollar) goes to about HK$7.7305, I think the HKMA (\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars, the trader said. Last Friday, as the U.S. dollar touched HK$7.7312, traders reported the HKMA buying small amounts of U.S. dollars for Hong Kong dollars. \par \par \uc2  A stronger stock market Monday may also be lending support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. At the midday close, Hong Kong's Hang Seng stock index was up 129.85 points to 11156.58 points. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-03-96 \par \par \uc2  0529GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3p02kq5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
