\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger -2: Small Investors, Speculators Burnt \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 04:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  He says smaller investors look to have been burnt this week, scrambling to cover short U.S. dollar positions at a loss as the U.K. banks and investment funds sold their U.S. dollars in favor of Hong Kong dollars. \par \par \uc2  'They had a strong selling interest on the top side. The 'TT' was dropping very fast, because they had already lengthened their positions from HK$7.7310 to HK$7.7330. Everyone else kept on buying. Then, suddenly, these large selling orders took place and the other buyers were forced to square,' the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer says. \par \par \uc2  He says the Hong Kong dollar appears to have hit a psychological barrier at current levels, with most participants concerned that they will see some sort of money or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the U.S. dollar weakens much further. \par \par \uc2  'So far, most of the traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will come out around the HK$7.7310 level,' he says. \par \par \uc2  But the head of treasury at a European bank says he has heard the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a buyer of Hong Kong dollars earlier this week to counter speculative U.S. dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  'It was probably some sort of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he says. 'All those speculators got burned.' \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on market rumors about its activities. \par \par \uc2  In money market activity so far Wednesday, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has injected a net HK$1.0 million, including the reversal of its discount window facility, the Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF). \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-03-96 \par \par \uc2  0353GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3d0288s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
