\par\par \b \uc2  HK says Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  pact will not affect reserves. \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Feb 20 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's agreement to act as Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  agent in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will not affect the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, an HKMA spokesman said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA would only act as an agent for the Bank of Japan, and so would not be putting its own money at risk, he said. \par \par \uc2  As an agent the HKMA would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if and when the Bank of Japan requested, the spokesman added. \par \par \uc2  However, he declined to go into details about where the HKMA would get the yen if asked to buy dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Most of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings of the local Exchange Fund, designed to back the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.8 to US$1, are denominated in U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  The fund's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets stood at US$51.8 billion at the end of September 1995. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA spokesman added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement with Japan would have no impact on other agreements aimed at maintaining the stability of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and banking systems that the HKMA has already signed with regional central banks. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA since November has signed bilateral repurchase agreements with Australia, Indonesia, Malaysia, Thailand, the Philippines and China allowing central banks to borrow from each other to bolster their reserves in times of crisis. \par \par \uc2  The spokesman said that the HKMA was discussing additional bilateral repurchase agreements with a number of other central banks, but declined to specify which ones. \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6441 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k0166x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
