\par\par \b \uc2  Japan announces Asian  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  pact. \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuter) - Japan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Singapore have reached an agreement which allows the Bank of Japan to ask its Asian counterparts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen trading on its behalf, Japan's Finance Ministry said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  News that the pact would be announced caused the dollar to surge against the yen earlier in the day, as dealers and economists said it signalled Japan's strong determination to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep Japan's fragile economic recovery on track. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which fell as low as 103.58 yen on Monday in overseas markets, jumped above 106 yen after the official announcement was made. \par \par \uc2  "I got a feeling that there is a really strong will of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan to push the dollar towards 110 yen," Makoto Kojima, director of Global Markets at Barclays Bank, told Reuters Financial Television. \par \par \uc2  That determination was also backed up by action, dealers said. The Bank of Japan appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least twice in Tokyo morning trade, initially buying dollars at above 104.45 yen then at around 105.30 yen just before midday in Tokyo, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan is keen to prevent its fragile economic recovery from being derailed by a strong yen, as it was last year after the dollar dropped to a postwar low of 79.75 yen last April. In February, the Finance Ministry announced deregulation measures aimed at boosting Japanese investment abroad, its second such package after similar steps were unveiled in August. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2k01611\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
