\par\par \b \uc2  HK interbank rates down as HKMA injects funds. \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Feb 8 (Reuter) - Interbank rates dropped on Friday as the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) injected HK$300 million into the interbank market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the HKMA likely moved to smooth the rise in the Hong Kong dollar, which has been crept higher in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  "The T.T. (Hong Kong dollar rate) is too strong. That's why they tried to push the short term interest rates lower to stop the speculation," said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Foreign inflows of funds to buy shares in the buoyant stock market have helped push up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight cash slipped to 4-3/4 5/8 percent from 4-15/16 7/8 mid-Thursday, and three-month cash eased to around 5-1/4 1/8 percent from 5-5/16 1/4. \par \par \uc2  In government paper, the one-week bill yield fell to 4.78 percent from five percent mid Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The long end was inspired by a firming in U.S. Treasury prices. Three-year notes were at 5.25 percent vs 5.32, five-year at 5.78 vs 5.86 percent and seven-year at 6.13 vs 6.19. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rate. It was little changed from Thursday at around HK$7.7310/15 to the U.S. dollar. -- HK Newsroom (852) 2843 6939 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2901k08\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
