\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Up On Fears Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1995\par 06:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-DJ)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is inching up Thursday, supported by market talk that the territory's quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be readying itself to buy an unspecified amount of Hong Kong dollars. \par \par \uc2  At 0456 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 7.7351 (Hong Kong) dlrs, down from HK$7.7357 around the same time Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'I heard the exchange fund was asking for (price) quotes from banks Wednesday,' which may have stirred some speculation that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was preparing to enter the market to buy Hong Kong dollars, says one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a regional Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  'I think the market now thinks they want it stable at current levels,' he adds. \par \par \uc2  Market players said there are also rumors the HKMA may be buying Hong Kong dollars as the government readies itself to make another injection into the territory's Provisional Airport Authority. The body responsible for building Hong Kong's new airport received its final stamp of approval from China Wednesday, and will become a full-fledged, rather than provisional, body from Friday. \par \par \uc2  The short-term demand for funds has been high recently, driving up short-term interest rates, partly as a result of escalating Sino-Taiwan tensions, he said. \par \par \uc2  A front-page story on Thursday's South China Morning Post says Chinese military authorities have prepared a plan to take over Taiwan if President Lee Teng-hui doesn't make major concessions on reunification if he is re-elected in March. \par \par \uc2  China's recent announcement that it plans to start extensive military exercises off the coast of Taiwan in February and March has also sparked nervousness. \par \par \uc2  The tension has led both Taiwanese investors and mainland Chinese banks to increase their buying of U.S. dollars, as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. \par \par \uc2  Thursday, however, the Hong Kong dollar selling has eased a bit, partly because of the fear of the HKMA, said the trader. \par \par \uc2  The approach of the year end has also increased the immediate demand for funds. \par \par \uc2  'With the position-squaring that comes with the month's end and the year's end, normally the demand for (U.S.) dollars is higher,' he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-11-95 \par \par \uc2  0509GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbu09hsf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
