\par\par \b \uc2  Asian Central Banks Add An  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Tool: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By JAMES T. AREDDY \par \uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1995\par 13:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-DJ)--Central banks in Asia on Monday said they created mechanisms to make their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more of a surprise and less disruptive to their investment portfolios. \par \par \uc2  Led by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the central banks of Australia, Indonesia, Malaysia and Thailand established bilateral credit lines of about U.S.$500.0 million each. \par \par \uc2  According to the agreements signed at a meeting of ten Asian central bankers in Hong Kong, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in need of U.S. dollars will pledge U.S. Treasurys to another, on a one-week, repurchase basis, for a quick cash injection. \par \par \uc2  'This action effectively gives the government a bigger pile of chips,' commented John Shilling, an economic adviser on Asian affairs at the World Bank in Washington. \par \par \uc2  The facilities will permit a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fortify its liquidity position quickly and quietly, and without permanently altering its portfolio of investments or causing disruption in the U.S. debt market - or its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as brokers register sudden adjustments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's holding of securities. \par \par \uc2  Gabriel Singson, of Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas, quipped that the terms are broadly similar between the various agreements - which weren't made public but were provided to AP-Dow Jones by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources. The simple language, Singson said, suggested that 'a lawyer possibly did not participate' in writing the terms. \par \par \uc2  Since the Mexican peso's collapse tarnished Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  last January, Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam has been busy culling opinion from his counterparts about how better to cooperate in driving out speculative forces. \par \par \uc2  When the Hong Kong dollar plunged as Mexico's woes seeped across the Pacific to the developing economies of Asia, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  orchestrated a quick doubling of interbank market rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1254GMT \par \par \uc2  1145 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbk097ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
