\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger; Under Pressure From U.S. Dlr Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 1995\par 05:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is at slightly stronger levels Thursday, but is coming under pressure from U.S. dollar buying interest by large local banks. \par \par \uc2  So far Thursday, the U.S. dollar has changed hands between $7.7319 (Hong Kong) and HK$7.7325. \par \par \uc2  At 0425 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7323, down from HK$7.7327 around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar had traded at slightly stronger levels around HK$7.7327 on Tuesday ahead of Wednesday's grave-sweeping holiday. \par \par \uc2  With local markets closed, investors in London's smaller U.S. dollar-Hong Kong dollar market took the opportunity to bid the U.S. dollar weaker, taking it to levels around HK$7.7315, according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The dealer says such a move had proved difficult in recent weeks, with corrections coming during Asian trading hours as investors remain concerned that too volatile a \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar would prompt market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar opened at HK$7.7319 in Hong Kong Thursday, but moved weaker as banks offered the U.S. dollar at quotes of HK$7.7322, HK$7.7323 and HK$7.7325. \par \par \uc2  'All those offers were swept out by the same guys,' the dealer says, noting large local banks have been aggressively buying the U.S. dollar on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dealer says he suspects the buying by large local players is a strategic move. \par \par \uc2  Participants have noted in recent days that a number of banks are holding on to longer U.S. dollar positions and that it would be in their interest to ensure the U.S. dollar-Hong Kong dollar spot rate, at least, remains stable at levels between HK$7.7320 and HK$7.7330 or moves even higher. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-11-95 \par \par \uc2  0438GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drb208lef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
