\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger, As Rates Slip On High Liquidity Levels \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 1995\par 05:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is holding at stronger levels in quiet trading Monday, with liquidity in the market at a high level as the stock market surges. \par \par \uc2  Data on Friday from the U.S. have given the market more reason to expect the Federal Reserve Board to cut interest rates again when it meets next month. As a result, Hong Kong markets are 'gradually reflecting' easier credit policy, says a dealer with a North American bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0340 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at $7.7310 (Hong Kong) dlrs, down from HK$7.7312 around the same time Friday. The range has been a minimal HK$7.7310 to HK$7.7315. \par \par \uc2  The dealer says the demand for Hong Kong dollars remains strong, but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to weaken much because of expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HK$7.7300. 'People are not willing to sell at HK$7.73 because they understand that is the bottom,' says the North American bank's dealer. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0346GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drag080y2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
