\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger After Talk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1995\par 07:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-DJ)--Talk of a warning shot from the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cooled the U.S. dollar after an early rise against its pegged Hong Kong counterpart Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at levels around $7.7450 (Hong Kong) and quickly worked its way up to HK$7.7465. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a local bank says that as the dollar moved above HK$7.7460, other participants told him the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled it preferred the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade at levels around HK$7.7450. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its specific activities in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants say they heard the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was offering to sell the U.S. dollar at HK$7.7450. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the local bank says that whether or not the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, talk that it had was enough to drop the dollar to levels as low as HK$7.7443. At 0505 GMT, the dollar has inched its way upward to HK$7.7445, a touch softer than HK$7.7450 around the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at another local bank says the dollar's downward move in mid-morning trading may have been due to stepped-up profit-taking by mainland Chinese banks ahead of a three-day weekend in the territory. \par \par \uc2  He says the Chinese banks were large buyers of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at weaker levels earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0506GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8p06h2q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
