\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker On U.S. Dollar's Rise Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1995\par 07:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar's rise against the Deutsche mark has touched off moderate selling of the Hong Kong dollar Wednesday, leading the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker against its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  So far Wednesday, the U.S. dollar, also known as the 'TT,' has traded between $7.7430 (Hong Kong) and HK$7.7450. At 0500 GMT, the dollar is quoted at HK$7.7443, up from HK$7.7435 around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a local bank says some investors are selling their Hong Kong dollars on Wednesday to buy U.S. dollars, hoping the U.S. unit continues to climb against the mark. \par \par \uc2  But he also sees significant commercially-driven U.S. dollar buying by 'a large Chinese bank' and several of the territory's biggest financial institutions. The buying began earlier this week, but was stepped up at the start of Asian trading on Wednesday, he says. \par \par \uc2  'This morning, one of the Chinese names bought the dollar from HK$7.7435,' the dealer says. 'We have a lot of demand .... A lot of local banks have to buy Japanese yen for customer needs. Due to this reason, they need to buy the U.S. dollar as a hedge. It's mainly for customer positions.' \par \par \uc2  The dealer says U.S. dollar demand should remain strong as long as the dollar holds firm against the mark. But concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the U.S. dollar rise too quickly, should cool demand slightly and cap the U.S. dollar at HK$7.7460 through the remainder of Asian trading hours Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0526GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8n06e9s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
