\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger As U.S. Dollar Holders Take Profits \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1995\par 06:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is at stronger levels after early profit-taking by U.S. dollar position holders early Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, also referred to as the 'TT,' opened at levels around HK$7.7445 Monday, but steadily worked its way down to HK$7.7423 as U.S. dollar positions holders closed out their positions and moved to the sidelines ahead of the Tuesday meeting of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy-making arm, according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a bank based in the territory. \par \par \uc2  'At the start of the morning, people were taking profits,' the dealer says. 'People are still waiting to see the direction of interest rates or to see if there's any change.' \par \par \uc2  The dealer says though he doesn't believe the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee will trim U.S. rates, investors are unwilling to get caught with large open positions after recent volatility in the Hong Kong dollar-U.S. dollar exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Because the Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar at a rate of HK$7.8000, local rates tend to shadow upward and downward adjustments of U.S. rates. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar volatility also has investors worrying about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA). The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in money markets during two spates of speculation in the past two weeks, pushing interbank rates to firmer levels above 6.00%. \par \par \uc2  'The interbank activity has calmed down, since people don't know how the (local) interest rates will go,' the dealer says. 'People still want to see if the HKMA restores (money market) funds.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0440GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8l06bhw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
