\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Despite Continued Demand, HIBOR Remain Firm \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1995\par 06:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is mildly weaker on Friday despite continued demand reflected in firm local money market rates. \par \par \uc2  So far Friday, the U.S. dollar, also called the 'TT,' has traded between $7.7438 (Hong Kong) and HK$7.7457. At 0430 GMT, the dollar is quoted at HK$7.7445, up from HK$7.7430 around the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has drifted weaker against the U.S. dollar on Friday in light trading as the U.S. unit remains relatively firm at levels above 97.00 yen, says the senior manager with an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  He says there is little news moving the Hong Kong dollar and he notes that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be 'consolidating for the time being in a new range' between HK$7.7375 per U.S. dollar and HK$7.7450 per U.S. dollar following a bout of speculation earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar moved sharply weaker against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, prompting a money market tightening defense by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'I think you can say the range is a bit wider than before. We may have a little room to move...following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he says. \par \par \uc2  There is some selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar by investors concerned about Sino-Taiwan tensions and leftover bearishness from a dire report on the territory's banking sector issued earlier this month by Moody's Investors Service Inc. \par \par \uc2  Still, demand for the Hong Kong dollar is seen remaining strong over the next several sessions as investors look to settle or switch from U.S. dollar positions taken earlier this week, the senior manager says. \par \par \uc2  As a result, local interbank rates should remain at levels close to or slightly above 6.00% over the next several sessions, he says. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0435GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8i06b58\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
