\par\par \b \uc2  HK govt paper ends stronger as local dlr stable. \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Aug 17 (Reuter) - Hong Kong Exchange Fund paper strengthened as the Hong Kong dollar stabilised against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said dealers. \par \par \uc2  One-week bills yielded 5.78 versus Wednesday's closing 5.88 percent, three-year notes yielded 6.68 versus 6.75 and five-year notes yielded 7.38 versus 7.47. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was HK$16.15 billion, down from Thursday's HK$24.63 billion. \par \par \uc2  "After the recent rise in the t.t. (Hong Kong to U.S. dollar exchange rate), the Hong Kong dollar has stabilised a bit," said a trader with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  He added that players had earlier feared the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the local dollar became as weak as 7.7450/60 to the U.S. dollar. The Hong Kong dollar traded at 7.7433/43 in late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates ended little changed after a quiet day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight ended at 6 5-7/8 percent versus Wednesday's closing 5-7/8 3/4 and three-month stood at 6 1/8 6 percent versus 6-3/16 1/4. \par \par \uc2  The closing balance in money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  was HK$1.22 billion. -- Kwan Chooi Tow (852) 2843 6936 (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8h05037\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
