\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Despite Heavy Demand, Rates Remain Firm \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1995\par 07:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is marginally weaker and money market rates remain firm at levels around 6.00% in quiet market conditions Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But participants say inactivity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets is misleading, as they're receiving a steady flow of Hong Kong dollar buy orders and U.S. dollar sell orders that they're having difficulty carrying out because of tight demand for the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  So far Tuesday, the U.S. dollar has traded between $7.7407 (Hong Kong) and HK$7.7417. At 0450 GMT, the dollar is quoted at HK$7.7415, slightly higher than HK$7.7410 around the same time Monday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a local bank says the U.S. dollar has been range-trading between HK$7.7395 and HK$7.7420 since early Monday, following largely successful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week. \par \par \uc2  He says local markets are quiet on Tuesday and that he expects the Hong Kong dollar to hold to its range over the next several sessions. \par \par \uc2  While markets are quiet, other participants say they're busy receiving orders to buy Hong Kong dollars against the U.S. dollar from overseas and local investors who took on U.S. dollar positions last week as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Because Hong Kong dollar rates are at attractive levels, some investors now want to hold both long- and shorter-term Hong Kong dollar positions, a dealer with a European bank says, creating heavy demand across the board and keeping interbank rates high. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0504GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8f0674a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
