\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Firmer After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Anti-Speculative Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1995\par 06:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is slightly firmer in quiet trading Monday, following largely successful \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets to counter speculation and cool the U.S. dollar late last week. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has so far Monday traded between $7.7395 (Hong Kong) and HK$7.7411. At 0407 GMT it is quoted at HK$7.7410, down from HK$7.7420 around the same time Friday. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) tightened local money markets and was seen buying Hong Kong dollars in the spot and forward markets to stem the dollar's rise against the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to levels as high as HK$7.7430 in early Friday trading, before easing to HK$7.7395 at the close of Asian trading hours on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar began to rise against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar following a Moody's report that predicted increasing speculation in the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the run-up to 1997, when China resumes sovereignty over Hong Kong. A flare-up in Sino-Taiwan relations was seen speeding speculative activity and the dollar's rise on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer says the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money market tightening on Friday, which lifted interbank rates well above 6.00%, sent a strong message to speculators and appears to have had the desired effect of cooling speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  'Most of the traders are worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA,' he says. 'This morning, most traders are staying on the sidelines and trying to minimize their transactions.' \par \par \uc2  He says local markets are quiet and should remain so throughout Monday, with the U.S. dollar trading between HK$7.7390 and HK$7.7420. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0421GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8e066cj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
