\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Following Moody's Report On HK Bank Sector \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 1995\par 07:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--A Moody's Investors Service Inc. report that raises questions about the long-term health of the territory's banking sector has dropped the Hong Kong dollar to slightly weaker levels against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  So far Wednesday, the U.S. dollar has traded between $7.7380 (Hong Kong) and HK$7.7398, but has spent most of Asian morning trading hours at the stronger end of the range. \par \par \uc2  At 0505 GMT, the dollar is quoted at HK$7.7395, up from HK$7.7387 around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Moody's issued a summary of its report on Hong Kong's banking industry earlier Wednesday. The report says the territory's banks face 'new challenges in a period of slowing economic growth, including tighter margins, more competition, slower loan growth and potential asset quality erosion.' \par \par \uc2  The report also predicts more speculation in Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future, similar to the speculative activity that moved the Hong Kong dollar to within HK$0.03 of its HK$7.8000 peg rate to the U.S. dollar in late January. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in January, temporarily raising interbank rates to choke off speculative activity. The report says higher rates would be detrimental to banks' growth. \par \par \uc2  The head of treasury at a European bank says the Moody's report 'stirred up' a bit of activity on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  With Hong Kong dollar rates remaining at a discount to comparable U.S. dollar rates, the report gave some investors a reason to resume interest rate arbitrage. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0514GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8906114\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
