\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Touches Weakest -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Not Seen In Mkts \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1995\par 06:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dealer says Wednesday's sudden upward movement of the U.S. dollar was unusual because local rates have been moving slightly upward to narrow their discount to U.S. rates ever since the U.S. Federal Reserve last Thursday signalled a 0.25 percentage point cut in the federal funds rate. \par \par \uc2  The buying interest at HK$7.7420 was also unusual, the dealer notes, since the U.S. dollar has been available at cheaper levels between HK$7.7350 and HK$7.7390 for the past several months. \par \par \uc2  Not since January, when the Hong Kong dollar moved to within HK$0.03 of its peg rate of HK$7.8000 per U.S. dollar, has Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at such weak levels. \par \par \uc2  Speculative activity then prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pulling the U.S. dollar back to levels around HK$7.7445 by January 20. \par \par \uc2  The treasury head says the U.S. dollar's strengthening hasn't prompted any activity by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) as far as he can tell. \par \par \uc2  He says dollar buying could be tied to local news reports that could be seen as unfavorable, both politically and economically, for Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  He says 'it could be the HKMA is quite relaxed' and won't be seen in the market unless or until the U.S. dollar again touches levels around HK$7.7700. But he stresses the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very real if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakens too quickly or too sharply. \par \par \uc2  'If it is moving too fast, they will come in at HK$7.7600,' he says. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0438GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7c057ze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
