\par\par \b \uc2  HK dollar barely moves after local rate hike. \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Feb 2 (Reuter) - The Hong Kong dollar, which has come under speculative attack recently, barely moved after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates on Thursday morning in line with Wednesday's hikes in U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  Acting on a public holiday, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the colony's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raised the Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF) rate or discount window by 0.5 percentage point, keeping pace with the rise in U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  It was the fourth rise in rates in the past year by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose main objective is to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability. \par \par \uc2  Though Hong Kong banks were officially closed for the three day Lunar New Year festivities, there has been some trading in Hong Kong dollars, said dealers working during the break. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was quoted on Thursday afternoon at HK$7.7320/40 to the U.S. dollar, little changed from HK$7.7315/35 on Monday ahead of the three-day holiday. \par \par \uc2  In mid January, the Hong Kong dollar was attacked when investors feared that all emerging markets could be unhinged by a Mexican-peso style financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced up interbank rates on at least three occasions to stem the colony's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar from an 18-month intra-day low of HK$7.7721. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's interest rates must track U.S. rates in order to maintain the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it increased the LAF by 0.5 percentage point effective immediately. \par \par \uc2  The LAF bid and offer rates were raised to 4.25 percent and 6.25 percent, from 3.75 percent and 5.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong rates were previously raised on November 16, 1994. \par \par \uc2  - HK Newsroom (852) 2843 6358 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr2201r93\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
