\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger; Buyers See Chances For Arbitrage \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1995\par 04:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--Probable arbitrage opportunities are keeping the Hong Kong dollar at stronger levels on Friday. \par \par \uc2  So far Friday, the U.S. dollar has traded between 7.7305 HK dlrs and 7.7320 HK dlrs. \par \par \uc2  At 0326 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 7.7320 HK dlrs, down from 7.7325 HK dlrs around the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The move isn't a significant one, but it continues a pattern of strengthening over the past several days. \par \par \uc2  The treasurer at an Asian bank says the Hong Kong dollar has stabilized 'quite a bit' over the past week because investors still believe the territory's quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step back into the money or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at any time. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets heavily over the past two weeks to push the Hong Kong dollar back to stronger levels after it moved to within 0.03 HK dlr of its peg rate of 7.8000 HK dlrs per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at various times seen draining money from the banking system to discourage lending, and buying Hong Kong dollars. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-01-95 \par \par \uc2  0346GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1r00gpf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
