\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Keeps Markets Tight \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 1995\par 03:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-DJ)--The Hong Kong dollar is trading at slightly stronger levels Wednesday, driven and held there by continuing money market tightness. \par \par \uc2  So far Wednesday, the U.S. dollar has traded in a relatively weak range between 7.7330 HK dlrs and 7.7351 HK dlrs. \par \par \uc2  At 0252 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 7.7340 HK dlrs, down from 7.7360 around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A local dealer in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also called the 'TT,' says the Hong Kong dollar is trading at stronger levels on Wednesday because shorter-term interest and interbank rates are being held at artificially high levels by the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets for nearly two weeks to stabilize the Hong Kong dollar after it slipped to within 0.03 HK dlrs of its peg rate of 7.8000 per U.S. dlr. \par \par \uc2  The dealer says that although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is calm on Wednesday, there is some buying interest in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'We can buy a cheap dollar,' the dealer says. \par \par \uc2  He says he expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep market liquidity tight, pushing shorter-term rates up and ensuring the U.S. dollar fluctuates only between 7.7300 HK dlrs and 7.7400 HK dlrs for the rest of the week. \pa