\par\par \b \uc2  HK Bank Transfers Traders -2: Losses Insignificant \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 1995\par 05:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'As the interest rates were pushed up last week, prices of these (Hong Kong dollar-denominated) notes went down and naturally we had bond losses on those positions,' according to Stuart Gulliver, head of treasury and capital markets at the bank. 'The loss may be a big amount to an individual trader but it is not material to HSBC Markets,' the group's dealing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Declining to offer specifics on the losses, Gulliver said the Hong Kong desk of HSBC Markets is profitable so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Gulliver said the traders were transferred laterally to other trading duties to relieve them of any stress that they would have suffered as a result of the losses. The practice is normal in a dealing room, said Gulliver. \par \par \uc2  His comments were carried in Thursday's editions of the South China Morning Post and were confirmed by a bank spokesman who was present at the English-language newspaper's interview with Gulliver. Gulliver couldn't immediately be reached for independent confirmation. \par \par \uc2  Hongkong Bank also denied that it was one of the speculators fueling the U.S. dollar's gains last week, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared to 7.7735 HK dlrs, its highest level in 18 months and within sight of the peg rate of 7.8000 HK dlrs. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market activity resulted in days of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which drained the local money market, sending interbank rates to double-digit levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  says the market is now 'returning to normal.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-01-95 \par \par \uc2  0421GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1j004n2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
