\par\par \b \uc2  HK interbank rates close firmer in cautious trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Jan 17 (Reuter) - Interbank rates finished firmer in cautious trading and bill/bond trading was volatile following fluctations in the Hong Kong dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rose to 6-1/2 six percent from 5-3/4 five and three month was 7-3/8 6-7/8 percent against 7-1/4 seven. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted two-way interest in the market with term rates going higher in the afternoon on the back of an easier Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to an intra-day low of 7.7475 to the U.S. dollar on rumours that China's paramount leader Deng Xiaoping had died, but it recovered to close at 7.7445/55. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was cautious on fears of HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  withdrew HK$848 million from the banking system, leaving the closing balance of the Exchange Fund at HK$2.13 billion after banks borrowed HK$1.85 billion from the discount window. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading of gvernment paper was volatile but the movement was exaggerated by thin volume. "The changes do not reflect the market situation but the position of individual traders." Five-year notes moved between 97.75 and 98.85 before ending at 98.15 to yield 8.81 percent vs 8.76 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The one-week bill yielded 5.90 percent compared with 6.40 on Monday and the three-year note yielded 8.35 against 8.40. \par \par \uc2  The newly tendered three-month bill yielded 6.20 percent against the average accepted tender yield of 6.19 earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said bidding interest had been dampened by the HKMA's repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the local dollar since last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Investors refrain from taking long-date paper amid the uncertain prospects of the Hong Kong dollar exchange rate," one said. "Year-end demand for the U.S. dollar should drag the local dollar down," he added. -- HK NEWSROOM (852) 2843 6369 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1h06y8p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
